;
YSEND - DOWNLOAD A FILE USING YMODEM

CALLER. Subject to current caller access policy.

A - Download a file using YMODEM

:A
DOWNLOAD A FILE USING YMODEM

    YSEND DU:filename

Sends a file from a readable directory to your terminal using YMODEM.

    YSEND A0:WELCOME.TXT
    YSEND P0:SIGMV011.LBR

Choose YMODEM receive in your terminal when the remote program is ready,
unless reception starts automatically. Select your local download
directory and wait for the transfer to finish.

The file must be on the currently mounted disk. Download permission
does not imply permission to execute that file on the RCP/M.

If the transfer appears to stall, check that the terminal is receiving
with YMODEM. Use its transfer-cancel facility and follow remote prompts
before retrying. Do not use text capture for binary files.

See HELP TRANSFER, HELP MOUNT and HELP LDIR.
